{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1417713-peach-homebrew-artifact-burnt-offering-\u2013-red-jade-dragon-sigh-wand-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022","id":1417713,"title":"[PEACH] Homebrew Artifact: Burnt Offering \u2013 (Red Jade Dragon Sigh Wand, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-11T15:09:24-07:00","id":1417713,"title":"[PEACH] Homebrew Artifact: Burnt Offering \u2013 (Red Jade Dragon Sigh Wand, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">So in my Dragon-Blooded game, one of the players approached me about making a 3-dot Dragon Sigh Wand... like three weeks ago.They gave me a grab-bag of powers, that I really didn't see a coherent theme for as a wishlist. The PC in question doesn't have the stats to drop a four dot artifact, and there are no published 3-dotters. Here's my revision of what the player wanted (I pulled the name off the Discord earlier today -- I'm not super attached). What do you all think?<br /> <br /> Awful first draft, skip to the next post:</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>[PEACH] Home-brew Artifact: Burnt Offering \u2013 (Red Jade Dragon Sigh Wand, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Crafted by Heptagram artificer Cynis Ganan, disciple of renowned firewand master, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Master Sakai of Kirighast, during the early stages of the Realm Civil War. This red jade Dragon Sigh Wand is deceptively simplistic in appearance: nearly five feet in length, but its unadorned barrel is only an inch across in diameter at its widest point. The barrel is beveled like a hypodermic needle, and sharpened to a needle\u2019s point. The stock is carved from skeletonized ironwood, and houses room for a single hearthstone. Numerous prayers, glyphs and blessings are carved on the inside of the weapon, but the outside is completely undecorated \u2013 every fitting serving an essential function.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The weapon incorporates brass from a neomah, brick powder from a powerful Fire Aspected manse on the Blessed Isle, and body parts from elementals of fire. It\u2019s most distinctive feature is its white jade receiver chamber, which allows the weapon to be reloaded from a breach rather than by the muzzle, which aides in aiming the weapon.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dedicated to Hesiesh, the Reciter of Loud Prayers and Efficacious Hymns, Burnt Offering is the perfect tool for creating ashes dedicated to the Dragons.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Attunement:</b> 5m</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Type: </b>Heavy (+14 DMG, OVW 5) </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Accuracy: </b>Close +1 (+3 bayonet); Short +5; (Medium +3; Long +1; Extreme \u22121)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Tags (firewand): </b>Lethal, Archery (Short), Flame, Slow</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Tags (bayonet):</b> Lethal, Melee, Piercing</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hearthstone slot(s):</b>1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Era:</b> Realm Civil War</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Evocations of Burnt Offering</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Burnt Offering is deliberately designed as a combination weapon: the sharpened barrel can be used as weapon with the stats of an artifact short-spear (medium weapon), and is explicitly compatible with martial arts styles which use the spear as a form weapon.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Further, whilst the lever-action of the weapons receiver does not remove the Slow tag from the weapon, it does make magic which enhances reloading more effective. If the wielder knows the Martial Arts Charm Cloud of Ebon Devils the difficulty to reload the weapon whilst aiming with enemies close by drops to 1. If the wielder uses specially prepared firedust shells (created as a Basic Project with an appropriate Craft), the Charm works automatically without a roll, regardless of the presence of enemies.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Burning Barrel</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost: </b>5m; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Type: </b>Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Keywords:</b> Uniform, Stackable</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Duration: </b>Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The barrel of Burnt Offering is the perfect means of delivering fire to its wielder\u2019s enemies, even when its fire is spent. This Evocation enhances a ranged attack made with a charge of firedust: the heat of the shot lingers on the barrel, increasing the damage of Withering attacks made with Burnt Offering\u2019s bayonet by +1 for the rest of the scene.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This Evocation may be stacked up to (Essence) times, but requires a charge of firedust to be expended on each activation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Blazing Shot</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost: </b>3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Type: </b>Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Duration: </b>Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>Burning Barrel</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Burnt Offering\u2019s strikes ignite flammable materials: a violent blaze instantly seeks to consume the struck object. This fire is natural, and may spread to surrounding objects or cause combustible materials to explode. When used in a decisive attack against a target, it adds one automatic success to the damage roll. If the attack does at least three health levels of damage, the target catches on fire, and must contend with (Wielder\u2019s Essence) lethal dice of damage every turn until he\u2019s able to extinguish himself. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">Loud Prayers</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Type:</b> Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Duration:</b> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The wielder extols the virtues of He Who Illuminates Both Worlds with Majesty and Power, drawing on Pasiap\u2019s ability to overcome all obstacles. Her attack ignores penalties from non-visual conditions such as high winds, bad weather, flawed ammunition, and so on.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If used in conjunction with an ammunition check, it reduces the penalty on check rolls to -1 per roll (instead of -2) as the user is able to bulk out their remaining firedust charges with common earth or sand.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Efficacious Hymns</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost: </b>3m; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Type:</b> Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Keywords: </b>Withering-only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Duration: </b>Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Loud Prayers</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Reciting a dedication to Hesiesh, Burnt Offer\u2019s wielder\u2019s Withering Attack Accuracy is calculated as if it were made from Short Range regardless of the distance she\u2019s firing from. Additionally, they may ignore up-to (Essence) in penalties from visual conditions (such as smoke, fog and darkness) as the rolling fire burns away all obscurities.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If used in conjunction with Loud Prayers, the cost of this Evocation is reduced to 1m.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">Steady Burn</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1i; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Type:</b> Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Keywords:</b> Perilous, Withering-only </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Duration:</b> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Efficacious Hymns and Burning Shot</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Advancing like a wild-fire, the wielder may Aim and take a move action in the same turn, and can Flurry an Aim with a Rush or Draw/Ready action. If she successfully Rushes or Draws Burnt Offering, she ignores the Defense penalty from taking these actions and Flurrying.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If Burnt Offing is already Readied, this Charm may instead be used to Reflexively Draw/Ready a different weapon instead, safely holstering Burnt Offering as part of the process.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Heavenly Smoke</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Type:</b> Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Keywords:</b> None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Duration:</b> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Burning Barrel</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This Evocation supplements a prayer roll \u2013 any formalized social influence roll against a god or similar spirit. The wielder touches Burnt Offering\u2019s barrel to a sacrifice worth up-to (Essence) Resource dots, and adds that many non-Charm successes to their roll as the offering burns to ash.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This Charm may only be used against the same spirit once per Story, unless reset by achieving a Legendary social goal then burning an offering to the spirit without making a social roll.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Firestorm Plume</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost: </b>8m, 3a, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Type: </b>Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Duration: </b>Instant </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Heavenly Smoke and Steady Burn</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Threading incendiary anima through her shot, the wielder unleashes a shot that erupts in a glorious blaze upon impact. After spending a turn Aiming, she makes a Decisive Attack, adding (Essence) dice of damage. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">On a hit, as long as she rolls at least one 10 on her attack or damage roll, the arrow explodes in an unblockable blast that extends out to short range from her target. All characters caught within it, including allies, must dodge her original attack roll or suffer dice of Hardness-ignoring lethal damage equal to the total 10s on both her attack roll and the original damage roll. The original target of her attack cannot dodge the blast. Any character that takes damage from the explosion is knocked prone and catches fire, suffering (Essence) further dice of lethal damage each turn until he extinguishes himself.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This Evocation may only be used once per scene.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Bleh. I hate it. It's trash.<br /> <br /> Okay... red jade flamethrower. Two Charm trees: the main tree of &quot;Flame&quot; focusing on decisive attacks and mobility, and the &quot;Prayer&quot; sub-tree which focuses on removing penalities and gods which gates the highest level Flame Charms. Explicitly written to complement Righteous Devil Style, so I've tried to avoid straight duplicate effects. It's still a bit scatty, but I'm happy it's not simply an &quot;Artifact means bigger numbers&quot; job. Any feedback would be gratefully received.<br /> <br /> Re-write below:</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-12-2020, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T03:31:37-07:00","id":1417785,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">[PEACH] Homebrew Artifact: Burnt Offering \u2013 (Red Jade Dragon Sigh Wand, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Crafted by Heptagram artificer Cynis Ganan, disciple of renowned firewand master, <span style=\"color:#000000\">Master Sakai of Kirighast, during the early stages of the Realm Civil War. This red jade Dragon Sigh Wand is deceptively simplistic in appearance: nearly five feet in length, but its unadorned barrel is only an inch across in diameter at its widest point. The barrel is beveled like a hypodermic needle, and sharpened to a needle\u2019s point. The stock is carved from skeletonized ironwood, and houses room for a single hearthstone. Numerous prayers, glyphs and blessings are carved on the inside of the weapon, but the outside is completely undecorated \u2013 every fitting serving an essential function.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The weapon incorporates brass from a neomah, brick powder from a powerful Fire Aspected manse on the Blessed Isle, and body parts from elementals of fire. It\u2019s most distinctive feature is its white jade receiver chamber, which allows the weapon to be reloaded from a breach rather than by the muzzle, which aides in aiming the weapon.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">A simple artifact focusing on the cleansing power of fire, and the unstoppable mobility of flame, Burnt Offering is dedicated to Hesiesh, the Reciter of Loud Prayers and Efficacious Hymns. It is the perfect tool for creating ashes dedicated to the Dragons.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Attunement:</b> 5m</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type (firewand): </b>Heavy (+14 DMG, OVW 5) </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type (bayonet): </b>Medium (+9 DMG, OVW 1, Defense +1)<br /> <b>Accuracy:</b> Close +1 (+2 bayonet); Short +5; (Medium +3; Long +1; Extreme \u22121)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Tags (firewand): </b>Lethal, Archery (Short), Flame, Slow</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Tags (bayonet):</b> Lethal, Melee, Piercing</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Hearthstone slot(s): </b>1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Era: </b>Realm Civil War</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Evocations of Burnt Offering</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Burnt Offering is deliberately designed as a combination weapon: the sharpened barrel can be used as weapon with the stats of a short-spear (medium weapon), and is explicitly compatible with martial arts styles which use the spear as a form weapon.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Further, whilst the lever-action of the weapons receiver does not remove the Slow tag from the weapon, it does make magic which enhances reloading more effective. If the wielder knows the Martial Arts Charm Cloud of Ebon Devils the difficulty to reload the weapon whilst aiming with enemies close by drops to 1. If the wielder uses specially prepared firedust shells (created as a Basic Project with an appropriate Craft), the Charm works automatically without a roll, regardless of the presence of enemies.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Certain Evocations of Burnt Offering generate a resource called <i>Blaze</i>. Blaze starts at 0 and is reset to 0 at the end of the scene; Burnt Offering\u2019s Blaze value may not be higher than the wielder\u2019s permanent Essence score (excess Blaze is lost). Some Evocations require a minimum Blaze to work \u2013 these are marked as \u201cBlaze X\u201d in their Keywords. Other Evocations might require spending points of Blaze as part of the Charm\u2019s cost.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Heavenly Smoke</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost: </b>3m; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type: </b>Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Keywords: </b>None </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Duration: </b>Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">This Evocation supplements a prayer roll \u2013 a formalized social influence roll (typically a bargain action) against a god or similar spirit. The wielder touches Burnt Offering\u2019s barrel to a sacrifice worth up-to (Essence) Resource dots, and adds that many non-Charm successes to their roll as the red jade ignites the sacrifice and burns it to a fine white ash.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Using this Evocation increases Burnt Offering\u2019s Blaze value by one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">This Evocation may only be used against the same spirit once per Story, unless reset by achieving a Legendary social goal then burning an offering to the spirit without making a social roll.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Loud Prayers</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type:</b> Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Keywords:</b> Uniform, Blaze 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Duration:</b> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Heavenly Smoke</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The wielder extols the virtues of He Who Illuminates Both Worlds with Majesty and Power, drawing on Pasiap\u2019s ability to overcome all obstacles. Their attack ignores up to (Essence) in penalties from non-visual conditions such as high winds, bad weather, flawed ammunition, and so on. If used against a spirit previously beseeched with Heavenly Smoke, ignore all non-visual penalties instead.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">If used in conjunction with an Ammunition Check, it reduces the penalty on check rolls to -1 per roll (instead of -2) as the user is able to bulk out their remaining firedust charges with common earth or sand (creating flawed ammunition). If the wielder has a relevant Craft Ability, this ammunition salvaging grants Craft points as a Basic Project on a successful Ammunition Check.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">If used in conjunction with Efficacious Hymns, the cost of this Evocation is reduced to 1m.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Efficacious Hymns</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Blaze 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Duration:</b> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Loud Prayers</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Reciting a dedication to Hesiesh, Burnt Offer\u2019s wielder\u2019s Withering Attack Accuracy is calculated as if it were made from Short Range regardless of the distance they're firing from.<br /> <br /> Additionally, they may ignore up to (Essence) in penalties from visual conditions (such as smoke, fog and darkness) as the rolling fire burns away all obscurities. If used against a spirit previously beseeched with Heavenly Smoke, ignore all visual penalties instead.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Burning Barrel</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost: </b>- (3m); <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type:</b> Permanant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Keywords: </b>Uniform, Stackable</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Duration: </b>Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The barrel of Burnt Offering is the perfect means of delivering fire to its wielder\u2019s enemies, even when its fire is spent. When Burnt Offering has Blaze 2+, its bayonet gains the statline of an Artifact Medium Weapon.<br /> <br /> Further, when the wielder makes a ranged attack made with a charge of firedust they may pay a 3m surcharge. If they do the heat of the shot lingers on the barrel, increasing Burnt Offering\u2019s Blaze value by one. This effect may be stacked once for each charge of firedust spent.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Blazing Shot</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost: </b>2m, Expend 1 Blaze; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type: </b>Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Duration:</b> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Burning Barrel</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Burnt Offering\u2019s strikes ignite flammable materials: a violent blaze instantly seeks to consume the struck object. This fire is natural, and may spread to surrounding objects or cause combustible materials to explode. When used in a decisive attack against a target, it adds one automatic success to the damage roll. If the attack does at least three health levels of damage, the target catches on fire, and must contend with (Wielder\u2019s Essence) lethal dice of damage every turn until he\u2019s able to extinguish himself. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Burning Charge</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost: </b>3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type:</b> Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-Only, Blaze 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Duration: </b>Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>Blazing Shot</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Targeting a foe at up to Short range, Burnt Offering's wielder charges forward to Close Range, impales a foe with their gun-barrel then unleashes a point blank shot. Make single Decisive Attack using Burnt Offering's bayonet, if it hits the attack inflicts an additional point of Onslaught Penalty, and adds (Blaze) bonus dice to the damage roll of the attack.<br /> <br /> If the wielder moves a range-band, this counts as their movement action for the round as well as their attack action.<br /> <br /> (Burnt Offering must be loaded in order to use this attack.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Steady Burn</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1i; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type:</b> Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Keywords:</b> Perilous</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Duration:</b> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Efficacious Hymns and Burning Charge</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Advancing like a wild-fire, the wielder may Aim and take a move action in the same turn, and can Flurry an Aim with a Rush or Draw/Ready action. If they successfully Rush, they ignore the Defense penalty from Flurrying and gains one Blaze. If they Draw/Readies Burnt Offering, they ignore the Defense penalties from Flurrying and the Draw/Ready action.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">If Burnt Offing is already Readied, this Evocation may instead be used to Reflexively Draw/Ready a different weapon, safely holstering Burnt Offering as part of the process.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Firestorm Plume</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost:</b> 8m, 3a, Expend all Blaze; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type:</b> Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Duration:</b> Instant </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Steady Burn</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Threading incendiary anima through their shot as they charge forward, the wielder unleashes a shot that erupts in a glorious blaze upon impact. This Evocation may only be used on the turn immediately after successfully Rushing a foe, after using the reflexive movement granted by a successful Rush, or after using Burning Charge; the wielder makes a Decisive Attack, adding (Essence) dice of damage. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">On a hit, as long as they roll at least one 10 on their attack or damage roll, the shot explodes in an unblockable blast that extends out to short range from the target. All characters caught within it, including allies but not the wielder themselves, must dodge the original attack roll or suffer dice of Hardness-ignoring lethal damage equal to the total 10s on both the attack roll and the original damage roll. The original target of the attack cannot dodge the blast. Any character that takes damage from the explosion is knocked prone and catches fire, suffering (Essence) further dice of lethal damage each turn until they extinguish themselves.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">This Evocation may only be used once per scene, but may be reset by building up to Blaze 3+.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-14-2020, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T13:03:32-07:00","id":1418238,"title":"","content":"Loud Prayers without Efficacious Hymns seems a little costly, I'd change it to 2m and put the 1m discount on it rather than Efficacious Hymns when used together (so it's still 4m for the combined effect).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T13:32:18-07:00","id":1418242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1417713-peach-homebrew-artifact-burnt-offering-\u2013-red-jade-dragon-sigh-wand-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022?p=1418238#post1418238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loud Prayers without Efficacious Hymns seems a little costly, I'd change it to 2m and put the 1m discount on it rather than Efficacious Hymns when used together (so it's still 4m for the combined effect).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the input! Yeah, I agree, that makes sense. Any other thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T07:13:06-07:00","id":1418359,"title":"","content":"I like it! I think I\u2019d need to see it in actual action to go beyond that because I don\u2019t see anything really crippling broken or OP here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T13:49:26-07:00","id":1418407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1417713-peach-homebrew-artifact-burnt-offering-\u2013-red-jade-dragon-sigh-wand-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022?p=1418242#post1418242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the input! Yeah, I agree, that makes sense. Any other thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>All in all its a pretty conservative artifact. which makes sense for a 3 dot.<br /> <br /> Firestorm Plume says targets 'must dodge the original attack roll' which I assume just means that its an unblockable attack but if you want to be super clear should just say that since technically you Evade rather than Dodge attacks.<br /> <br /> Oh and Firestorm Plume Expends all Blaze, but doesn't actually require you to have any blaze to use it, which might be unintended/confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T15:02:29-07:00","id":1418433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1417713-peach-homebrew-artifact-burnt-offering-\u2013-red-jade-dragon-sigh-wand-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022?p=1418359#post1418359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it! I think I\u2019d need to see it in actual action to go beyond that because I don\u2019t see anything really crippling broken or OP here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an essay due next week (so if I'm on the forums more than usual, it's because I'm procrastinating). Once that's done, I'll do an areana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1417713-peach-homebrew-artifact-burnt-offering-\u2013-red-jade-dragon-sigh-wand-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022?p=1418407#post1418407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All in all its a pretty conservative artifact. which makes sense for a 3 dot.<br /> <br /> Firestorm Plume says targets 'must dodge the original attack roll' which I assume just means that its an unblockable attack but if you want to be super clear should just say that since technically you Evade rather than Dodge attacks.<br /> <br /> Oh and Firestorm Plume Expends all Blaze, but doesn't actually require you to have any blaze to use it, which might be unintended/confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firestorm Plume says &quot;<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">the shot explodes in an unblockable blast</span></span></span>&quot; which I thought was pretty clear. :P<br /> <br /> (Note the initial attack isn't unblockable, only the explosion.)<br /> <br /> I'm not against using Firestorm Plume as an alpha strike before building up any Blaze, which is why I didn't put a minimum on it. You could nix the &quot;1/scene&quot; limitation and just make it Blaze 3. But requiring three Withering attacks before you can use it (or a prayer, a Withering attack, and a Rush) seemed like it wouldn't see use in 90% of fights -- which kinda sucks. If you've invested all the way up to the capstone, you should be able to use it, I figure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T15:37:16-07:00","id":1418441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1417713-peach-homebrew-artifact-burnt-offering-\u2013-red-jade-dragon-sigh-wand-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022?p=1418433#post1418433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Firestorm Plume says &quot;<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">the shot explodes in an unblockable blast</span></span></span>&quot; which I thought was pretty clear. :P<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it does, my B.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1417713-peach-homebrew-artifact-burnt-offering-\u2013-red-jade-dragon-sigh-wand-artifact-\u2022\u2022\u2022?p=1418433#post1418433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not against using Firestorm Plume as an alpha strike before building up any Blaze, which is why I didn't put a minimum on it. You could nix the &quot;1/scene&quot; limitation and just make it Blaze 3. But requiring three Withering attacks before you can use it (or a prayer, a Withering attack, and a Rush) seemed like it wouldn't see use in 90% of fights -- which kinda sucks. If you've invested all the way up to the capstone, you should be able to use it, I figure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I think that's fine, just that it might make some people think it requires at least 1 Blaze while others will think it doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}